      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.1: Number of community-based resilience-building initiatives implemented that incorporate gender-responsive risk reduction and resilience-building measures.</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Develop, strengthen, or review national or local guidelines/tools/approaches on community-based resilience building by mainstreaming dedicated measures that foster gender equality1, DRR, CCA, and other risk reduction interventions as indicated by the local context and ensure they are informed by multidimensional risk and gender analyses.

Strengthen the capacities and skills of men and women in local government and civil society to foster gender equality at scale, with an emphasis on women&#x2019;s empowerment, leadership, and inclusiveness, in community-based resilience-building programs.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2025-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="5"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of men/women practitioners and decision-makers from national and local institutions trained to consider DRR and CCA in their development planning processes.</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Practitioners and decision-makers from national and local institutions trained to consider DRR and CCA in their development planning processes</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2025-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="100"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of applications of sex-age-disability disaggregated damage and loss information in development and recovery planning, policymaking, monitoring, and reporting</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support the digitalization and institutionalization of sex-age-disability disaggregated damage &amp; loss tracking systems by establishing or expanding existing databases into full-fledged systems that capture damage and loss arising from disaster and climate change impacts to inform national risk profiles.
Strengthen sex-age-disability disaggregated data collection and analysis capacity of key stakeholders to be able to feed into damage and loss tracking systems, risk assessments, and other hazard-specific research products.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2026-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2026-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="2"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of men and women local decision makers and practitioners trained to implement gender-responsive community-based resilience programs that foster women&#x2019;s leadership and empowerment.</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support the implementation of community-based resilience-building interventions to foster gender equality benefitting women and girls, children and youth, persons with disabilities, and socio-economically marginalized groups, as part of local government plans, budgets, and reporting requirements.</narrative>
    </description>
